# Cross-origin isolation. Required, not optional.
#
# SharedArrayBuffer is the transport for the timing data shared between the
# main thread, the AudioWorklet and the ScoringWorker. Browsers only expose it
# to a cross-origin-isolated context, which needs BOTH headers below. Without
# them `new SharedArrayBuffer(...)` throws and the app does not start.
#
# vite.config.ts sets these for `vite dev` and `vite preview`. That plugin does
# NOT run in production — a static host serves dist/ and knows nothing about
# Vite. This file is how the host is told.
#
# Netlify and Cloudflare Pages read public/_headers automatically; Vite copies
# it to dist/ verbatim. On any other host it is inert documentation and the
# equivalent must be configured by hand:
#
#   nginx     add_header Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy same-origin;
#             add_header Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy require-corp;
#   Apache    Header set Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy "same-origin"
#             Header set Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy "require-corp"
#   Vercel    "headers" in vercel.json
#
# This file does not decide D3 (hosting). It makes two of the candidates work
# and records what the rest have to do.
#
# Verify against a real build with `npm run check:isolation`.

/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
